# Slice 283 probe: code over immutable data writes a char place by its bare name: a working cell with no value record?  Entry 7.
Data:
    char: x 'A'
    var:
        char: x 'a'
    end: var
end: Data
WritesChar:
    x: 66
    var:
        char: x 'c'
    end: var
end: WritesChar
@: held_char WritesChar
fn: write_char (@: d Data) int
    ---
        call: held_char d
        return: 90
        catch: interpreter ()
            return: 1
    ---
end: write_char
fn: m () int
    d: immutable: merge(Data)
    return: write_char(d)
end: m
int: code 7
if: m() != 1
    code: 11
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
